Z||000000||AkursedX||12-22-2001||02:21 PM||||Hi, I just wanted to post a couple pics of my 87GT with it's new winter rims and tires.<P>I'm a big fan of black rims and since these GT rims were really beat up, I decided to sandblast them and paint them all black.  <P>Personally, I really like how it came out.  I think if the car was lowered an inch or two, and had a red neon kit underneath it, it would probably look really neat.  But this is my winter car, so I can't afford such luxuries  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>Sorry for not having time to wash the car though, plus it's just took cold out!<P>But anyways, I just wanted to know what people thought of the new look  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/PC210012.JPG"> <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/PC210013.JPG"> <P>------------------<BR><BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sigpic2_2.jpg"> ||||reg||7
Z||000001||Formula88||12-22-2001||02:40 PM||||Sorry, don't care for it much - too much black.  It looses the lines with no contrast.  Perhaps some chrome lug nuts would help?  <P>I really love the look of the OEM GT rims with the black center and polished rims, so I'm a bit prejudiced, I guess.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000002||bocefas||12-22-2001||02:43 PM||||I like it, I like it....perhaps if you left the polished rims on the wheels it would be a little better, but I think all in all it looks pretty tough.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Raydar||12-22-2001||03:30 PM||||Darth Vader. Your car is ready. Darth Vader...<BR>Very sinister looking. <BR>I like it. I might be tempted to polish the very lip (3/16" edge) of the wheel. Not the entire outer rim, though.<P>------------------<BR>Raydar<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><BR>From the Department of Redundancy Department.</FONT>||||reg||14
