Z||000013||AkursedX||12-22-2001||10:22 PM||||Thanks for the responses everyone!  <P>More or less, I got the type of response I figured I would get.  It is definietly a unique taste.  <P>I had the center caps painted black as well, but I didn't like how it looked, so I went back to chrome with those.  <P>Chrome lugnuts might be a good idea, same with that Idea of polishing the very outer-lip of the rim.  But those rims are probably going to stay the way they are.<P>But I think I did a good job achieving the look I wanted.  I wanted a Darth-Vader type of car.  And it looks especially mean at night.  Not only is the car black, and the rims are black, the windows are also tinted!  Like I said in my previous post, if it was lowered and had a red neon kit underneath it, it would sweet, at least in my eyes.  But that's not going to happen.  I gotta save my money for my new engine in my 88  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/cool.gif">||||reg||1
